IMPORT prelude

-- Health Promotion Board Act 2001 (Singapore) -- the Board's functions as they reach the public (s 11(1)(g), (3)), the acts
-- needing the Minister's approval (ss 12(b), (c), 22, 41), the meeting rules (ss 7, 9), protection from personal liability and
-- for public information (s 16), the financial year (s 18), the 2001 transfer of Government staff and their pension (ss 31-33),
-- and the three provisions that reach the public as offences: misuse of the Board's symbol (s 38), secrecy (s 39) and
-- composition (s 40).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/HPBA2001.txt. The deposit
-- says it "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the
-- latest amending Act annotated in the text is Act 11 of 2019 (at s 11(1)); Act 5 of 2018 is annotated throughout.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0172 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has
-- asked a sharper question yet. The answer the text gives is: very little directly. It is an institutional Act that creates the
-- Board (which runs school health and dental services and sets dietary guidelines) and gives it functions; it confers no right
-- to any service and s 11(3) says its functions create no duty enforceable in court. SCOPED to the rules with decision content.
-- Not encoded: the seal and execution of instruments (s 4), the constitution and appointments (ss 5, 6, 8) beyond s 7, the
-- general functions and powers in ss 11(1) and 12 except those listed above, committees and delegation (ss 13, 14), staff
-- (s 15), estimates, funds, grants, shares, bank accounts, application and investment of funds (ss 19-25), the transfer of
-- property, contracts and proceedings (ss 30, 34-36), regulations beyond the approval requirement (s 41), the saving (s 42) and
-- the Schedule of former departments.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Health Promotion Board Act 2001 -- the Board`

§§ `11(1)(g), 11(3) -- services, and no enforceable duty`

-- s 11(1)(g): a function of the Board is "to provide healthcare services (including medical, dental, health-screening and
-- immunisation services) to school children and such other persons or class of persons as the Board thinks fit".
-- s 11(3): "Nothing in this section is to be construed as imposing on the Board, directly or indirectly, any form of duty or
-- liability enforceable by proceedings before any court."
-- So a school child is within the class the Board serves by statute; anyone else only if the Board thinks fit. Neither has a
-- claim in court to the service.
GIVEN `is a school child` IS A BOOLEAN, `is in a class the Board thinks fit to serve` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is within the class the Board serves` IF
    `is a school child` OR `is in a class the Board thinks fit to serve`

GIVEN `is a school child` IS A BOOLEAN, `is in a class the Board thinks fit to serve` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person can enforce the service in court under section 11` IF
    FALSE

-- s 12(h): the Board may "charge fees or commissions for services rendered by the Board or for the use of any of its facilities".
-- The Act sets no fee and no exemption; nothing in it says school health services are free.

§§ `12, 22, 41 -- what needs the Minister`

-- s 12: "power to do anything" for its functions, and in particular may (a) enter contracts; (b) "with the approval of the
-- Minister, acquire and hold such movable or immovable property"; (c) "with the approval of the Minister, form or participate in
-- the formation of any company, partnership or joint venture"; (h) charge fees; (l) grant loans to staff "for any purposes
-- specifically approved by the Board". s 22: raise loans "from the Government or, with the consent of the Minister, from any
-- other source". s 41: make regulations "with the approval of the Minister".
DECLARE Step IS ONE OF
    `entering into a contract`
    `acquiring property`
    `forming a company or joint venture`
    `charging fees for its services`
    `granting a loan to an employee`
    `borrowing from the Government`
    `borrowing from a bank`
    `making regulations`

GIVEN `the step` IS A Step
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister's approval is needed` IF
    CONSIDER `the step`
    WHEN `acquiring property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `forming a company or joint venture` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `borrowing from a bank` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `making regulations` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `7 -- term of office and resignation`

-- s 7(1): a member (including the Chairperson) holds office "for such term, not exceeding 3 years, as the Minister specifies in
-- the appointment, and may be re-appointed".
GIVEN `term in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the term of appointment is permitted` IF
    `term in years` > 0 AND `term in years` <= 3

-- s 7(2): a member "may resign from his or her office at any time by giving at least one month's notice in writing to the
-- Minister". Notice is counted here in months.
GIVEN `notice in months` IS A NUMBER, `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `given to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the resignation notice is sufficient` IF
    `notice in months` >= 1 AND `in writing` AND `given to the Minister`

§§ `9 -- meetings`

-- s 9(1): "At all meetings of the Board, 5 members form a quorum."
GIVEN `members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the meeting is quorate` IF
    `members present` >= 5

-- s 9(4): questions are "decided by a majority of votes of the members present and voting". (5): the person presiding "has a
-- deliberative vote and, in the case of an equality of votes, he or she also has a casting vote". The votes counted below already
-- include the presiding member's deliberative vote. Treating a decision at an inquorate meeting as not carried is an inference
-- from s 9(1); the Act states no consequence.
GIVEN `members present` IS A NUMBER, `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `casting vote for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the question is carried` IF
        `the meeting is quorate` `members present`
    AND (    `votes for` > `votes against`
         OR (`votes for` = `votes against` AND `casting vote for`))

§§ `16 -- protection from personal liability, and for public information`

-- s 16(1): "No suit or other legal proceedings shall lie personally against any member, officer or employee of the Board or other
-- person acting under the direction of the Board for anything which is in good faith done or intended to be done in the
-- execution or purported execution of this Act or any other written law."
GIVEN `is a member, officer, employee or person directed by the Board` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted in executing or purportedly executing a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a personal suit is barred` IF
        `is a member, officer, employee or person directed by the Board`
    AND `acted in good faith`
    AND `acted in executing or purportedly executing a written law`

-- s 16(2): where the Board "provides a service to the public by which information is supplied to the public", neither the Board
-- nor its employees "shall be liable for any loss or damage suffered by any member of the public by reason of any error or omission
-- of whatever nature appearing in the information or however caused if made in good faith and in the ordinary course of the
-- discharge of the duties of such employees". Unlike (1), this protects the Board itself. Dietary guidelines and nutritional
-- information (s 11(1)(f)) are an obvious case; that they are such a "service" is an inference.
GIVEN `the information was supplied to the public as a service` IS A BOOLEAN, `the error was made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the ordinary course of duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board is shielded from liability for the information error` IF
        `the information was supplied to the public as a service`
    AND `the error was made in good faith`
    AND `in the ordinary course of duties`

§§ `18 -- financial year`

-- s 18: the financial year "begins on 1 April of each year and ends on 31 March of the succeeding year". A financial year is named
-- here by the calendar year in which it begins.
GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER, `month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the financial year beginning in` MEANS
    IF `month` >= 4 THEN `calendar year` ELSE `calendar year` - 1

§§ `31-33 -- Government staff transferred on 1 April 2001`

-- s 31(1): persons employed by the Government immediately before 1 April 2001 in a department in the Schedule (National Health
-- Education Department, Department of Nutrition, School Health Service, School Dental Service, Health Promotion Division
-- Administration) "are transferred to the service of the Board on terms no less favourable than those enjoyed by them immediately
-- prior to their transfer".
GIVEN `was employed by the Government immediately before 1 April 2001` IS A BOOLEAN, `in a department in the Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person was transferred to the Board` IF
    `was employed by the Government immediately before 1 April 2001` AND `in a department in the Schedule`

-- s 32(2): any term relating to length of service "must recognise the length of service of the persons so transferred while in
-- the employment of the Government to be service with the Board".
GIVEN `was transferred` IS A BOOLEAN, `years with the Government` IS A NUMBER, `years with the Board` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the recognised years of service` MEANS
    IF `was transferred` THEN `years with the Government` + `years with the Board` ELSE `years with the Board`

-- s 32(4): the Government "is liable to pay to the Board such portion of any pension, gratuity or allowance payable to the person
-- on his or her retirement as the same bears to the proportion which the aggregate amount of his or her pensionable emoluments
-- during his or her service with the Government bears to the aggregate amount of his or her pensionable emoluments during his or
-- her service under both the Government and the Board". The sentence is tangled ("as the same bears to the proportion"); it is
-- read here as the Government share being the pension times Government emoluments over total emoluments. That reading is an
-- inference.
GIVEN `the pension` IS A NUMBER, `Government emoluments` IS A NUMBER, `Board emoluments` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Government's share of the pension` MEANS
    IF `Government emoluments` + `Board emoluments` > 0
    THEN `the pension` * `Government emoluments` / (`Government emoluments` + `Board emoluments`)
    ELSE 0

-- s 33: "Despite the provisions of the Pensions Act 1956, no person who is transferred to the service of the Board under section 31
-- is entitled to claim any benefit under that Act on the ground that he or she has been retired from the service of the Government
-- on account of abolition or reorganisation of office in consequence of the establishment and incorporation of the Board."
GIVEN `was transferred` IS A BOOLEAN, `claims on the ground of abolition or reorganisation caused by the Board's creation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the abolition-of-office claim is barred` IF
    `was transferred` AND `claims on the ground of abolition or reorganisation caused by the Board's creation`

§§ `38 -- the Board's symbol`

-- s 38(1): the Board "has the exclusive right to the use of such symbol or representation as it may select or devise". (2): any
-- person who uses a symbol or representation "identical with that of the Board, or which so resembles the Board's symbol or
-- representation as to deceive or cause confusion, or to be likely to deceive or to cause confusion" is guilty of an offence: fine
-- not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 6 months or both. No intent is mentioned.
GIVEN `used a symbol` IS A BOOLEAN, `identical to the Board's` IS A BOOLEAN, `resembles it so as to deceive or confuse, or be likely to` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the symbol offence is committed` IF
        `used a symbol`
    AND (`identical to the Board's` OR `resembles it so as to deceive or confuse, or be likely to`)

§§ `39 -- secrecy`

-- s 39(1): "Except for the purpose of the performance of his or her duties or the exercise of his or her functions or when
-- lawfully required to do so by any court or where required or allowed by any written law", a person who "is or has been" a
-- member, officer, employee or agent of the Board or a member of a committee must not disclose information "relating to the
-- affairs of the Board or of any other person" obtained in the performance of duties. (2): fine not exceeding $2,000 or
-- imprisonment not exceeding 12 months or both.
DECLARE Disclosure
    HAS `by a present or former member, officer, employee, agent or committee member` IS A BOOLEAN
        `of information obtained in performing duties` IS A BOOLEAN
        `for performing duties or functions` IS A BOOLEAN
        `lawfully required by a court` IS A BOOLEAN
        `required or allowed by a written law` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the secrecy offence is committed` IF
        `the disclosure`'s `by a present or former member, officer, employee, agent or committee member`
    AND `the disclosure`'s `of information obtained in performing duties`
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `for performing duties or functions`)
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `lawfully required by a court`)
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `required or allowed by a written law`)

§§ `38(2), 39(2) -- maximum penalties`

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `misusing the Board's symbol`
    `breaching secrecy`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `misusing the Board's symbol` THEN 10000
    WHEN `breaching secrecy` THEN 2000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `misusing the Board's symbol` THEN 6
    WHEN `breaching secrecy` THEN 12

§§ `40 -- composition`

-- s 40(1): "The Chief Executive or any officer authorised by the Chief Executive may compound any offence under this Act that is
-- prescribed as a compoundable offence by collecting from a person reasonably suspected of having committed the offence a sum of
-- money not exceeding $1,000." (2): on payment "no further proceedings are to be taken against that person in respect of the
-- offence". No offence is prescribed in the Act itself; prescription would be by regulations (s 41(b)), none of which was read.
GIVEN `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `by the Chief Executive or an officer authorised by the Chief Executive` IS A BOOLEAN, `sum collected` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the composition is lawful` IF
        `the offence is prescribed as compoundable`
    AND `by the Chief Executive or an officer authorised by the Chief Executive`
    AND `sum collected` > 0
    AND `sum collected` <= 1000

GIVEN `the composition was lawful` IS A BOOLEAN, `the sum was paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `further proceedings are barred` IF
    `the composition was lawful` AND `the sum was paid`
